    linkLabel: "Visit Kenosha",
    placeName: "Kenosha",
    stateName: "Wisconsin",
    title: "Kenosha on Lake Michigan",
    dek: "Culinary tradition and community pride along Wisconsin’s lakeshore.",
    heroImage: "/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/01-img-8897-kenosha-public-museum.jpg",
    gallery: ["/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/02-y26a0897-enhanced-nr-villa-d-carlo.jpg","/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/03-y26a0965-enhanced-nr-villa-d-carlo.jpg","/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/04-kenosha-public-museum-2.jpg","/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/05-electricstreetcar-e-electric-streetcar.jpg","/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/06-191023-miner-267.jpg","/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/07-2024-06-11-vk-fishing-32-kenosha-charter-boat-association.jpg","/destinations/spring-2026-web/visit-kenosha/08-img-2324-pleasant-prairie-premium-outlets.jpg"],
    paragraphs: [
      "Nestled along the shores of Lake Michigan, Kenosha is a destination where culinary tradition and community pride are deeply intertwined—especially when it comes to Italian cuisine. With roots tracing back to waves of Italian immigrants who settled here in the late 19th and early 20th centuries, Kenosha has cultivated a food culture that feels both authentic and warmly Midwestern. Today, visitors can taste that legacy in everything from family-run restaurants to beloved neighborhood markets.",
      "Kenosha’s Italian heritage is not just preserved—it’s celebrated. The city maintains a meaningful connection with its sister city, Cosenza, reinforcing cultural ties that continue to influence local traditions, cuisine, and community events. Each September, that heritage comes alive during the annual Kenosha Italian Festival, where the aromas of garlic, simmering sauces, and carefully curated wines unite families, friends, and visitors alike.",
      "Attendees can expect live music, dancing, and an abundance of classic Italian dishes served with unmistakable pride. One of the defining features of the region’s food scene is the unique style of pizza found throughout southeastern Wisconsin. Known for its thin, crisp crust and square-cut “party slices,” this style encourages sharing—perfectly reflecting the communal spirit of Italian dining.",
      "At Cut Stone, that tradition is elevated with wood-fired techniques honoring the Neapolitan style of pizza that produces perfectly blistered crusts and deeply flavorful pies. Each bite balances rustic simplicity with artisan craftsmanship, making it a must-visit for pizza enthusiasts. For a more coastal Italian experience, Tuscany Bistro Bar & Grill offers a menu inspired by Tuscan flavors and an emphasis on seafood specialties.",
      "Dishes here highlight fresh ingredients, delicate preparation, and a refined approach to traditional recipes. It’s a reminder that Italian cuisine is as diverse as the regions it comes from—and Kenosha embraces that diversity beautifully. Equally important to the city’s culinary identity are its multi-generational family establishments. Casa Capri, Villa D'Carlo, Tenuta's Restaurant, and Infusino's have each built loyal followings over decades.",
      "These restaurants are known for generous portions, time-honored recipes, and the kind of hospitality that makes every guest feel like family. Meals here are not rushed—they’re meant to be savored, shared, and remembered. At the heart of Kenosha’s Italian-American community is the Italian American Club of Kenosha. More than just a gathering place, the club serves as a steward of cultural traditions, hosting events, celebrations, and meals that keep heritage alive for future generations.",
      "Whether attending a festive dinner event or a lively party, visitors can experience firsthand the warmth and pride that define Kenosha’s Italian roots. No culinary tour of Kenosha would be complete without a stop at Tenuta's Delicatessen & Liquor. This iconic market is a destination in itself, offering everything from freshly prepared foods and imported ingredients to fine wines and specialty gifts.",
      "The moment you walk through the doors, you’re greeted by an unforgettable aroma—a blend of cured meats, aged cheeses, fresh bread, and spices that instantly transports you to an old-world Italian marketplace. It’s the kind of place where browsing turns into tasting, and tasting turns into a full basket of culinary treasures. While Italian cuisine may be the soul of Kenosha’s dining scene, the city’s offerings extend far beyond.",
      "Visitors can explore classic diners serving hearty breakfasts, traditional Wisconsin supper clubs known for their cocktails and comfort food, modern sushi bars, cozy cafés, and inventive eateries that reflect a growing culinary diversity. In Kenosha, every meal tells a story—but its Italian heritage ensures those stories are always rich, flavorful, and deeply rooted in tradition. Beyond the table, Kenosha offers a wide array of experiences that make it a well-rounded travel destination.",
      "Visitors can head out onto Lake Michigan for charter fishing excursions, explore more than a half-dozen museums and art galleries that showcase everything from local history to contemporary works, or spend a day on one of the area’s beautifully maintained golf courses. The city also features a variety of entertainment spaces—from live music venues and theaters to waterfront parks and seasonal festivals—ensuring there’s always something to see and do between meals.",
    ],
